    content: `## Understanding Material Demands in Solventless Lamination

Flexible packaging converters continually debate the ideal material formulation for side containment dams. A solventless lamination dam operates in an aggressive environment:

- Direct contact with exothermic 2-component polyurethane resins.
- High rotational speeds (300 to 600 m/min).
- Friction against both hard chromium steel and elastomer rubber rolls.
- Exposure to harsh cleaning solvents such as ethyl acetate, MEK, and acetone.

Choosing the incorrect fluoropolymer grade leads either to roller damage, premature edge leakage, or compliance violations in food-grade packaging lines.

## Material Comparison Matrix

| Property | Virgin PTFE | 15% Glass-Filled PTFE | Bronze-Filled PTFE | Reprocessed PTFE |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Coefficient of Friction** | 0.04 – 0.08 | 0.12 – 0.18 | 0.14 – 0.20 | 0.10 – 0.15 |
| **Shore D Hardness** | 55 – 60 | 62 – 68 | 68 – 72 | 50 – 58 |
| **Roller Abrasion Risk** | Zero (Safe) | Moderate / High | Severe (Avoid) | Variable / High |
| **FDA Food Contact** | Certified Compliant | Restricted | Non-Compliant | Non-Compliant |
| **Dimensional Stability** | High (Annealed) | Very High | Excellent | Low (Prone to creep) |

## Preventing Metering Roller Scoring and Chromium Damage

Chromium-plated metering rollers and specialized NBR rubber sleeves cost thousands of dollars to recoat and ground-grind. When glass-filled or bronze-filled Teflon compounds are used:

1. Microscopic glass fiber shards emerge as the matrix wears down.
2. These hard ceramic shards act as cutting teeth against the rotating roller.
3. Fine circumferential score lines form on the roll face, permanently ruining coating laydown uniformity.

**Pure Virgin PTFE** exhibits a yield strength that conforms elastoplastically to the roller surface, creating an impermeable seal while shielding expensive tooling from scratches.

## Temperature Stability & Solvent Resistance

Virgin PTFE maintains complete mechanical integrity across a working thermal envelope from -200°C to +260°C. Since solventless PU adhesives operate between 35°C and 55°C, Virgin PTFE remains well within its elastic stability window without softening, blistering, or leaching additives.`,
